.TH SOJU-TUI-SETUP 8 "2026-08-27" "soju-tui" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
soju-tui-setup \- explicitly configure local access to Soju's admin socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo soju-tui-setup
.BI --user " login"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soju-tui-setup
discovers Soju's administrative Unix socket, previews a per-user ACL, and asks
before granting the selected trusted local account access. On systemd hosts it
installs a path unit that reapplies the ACL when Soju recreates the socket.
.PP
The Debian package does not run this command automatically. Installing,
upgrading, or removing the package does not modify Soju, its configuration, its
database, its users, socket ACLs, or systemd units.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --user " login"
Local account to authorize. Required when it cannot be inferred from sudo.
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Soju configuration path. The default is
.IR /etc/soju/config .
.TP
.BI --socket " path"
Override the administrative socket discovered from the Soju configuration.
.TP
.BI --sojuctl " path"
Override the discovered sojuctl executable.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Display the discovered settings and proposed ACL units without changing them.
.TP
.B --yes
Accept package and ACL confirmation prompts.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Display command usage.
.SH SECURITY
Access to Soju's administrative socket grants control over all Soju users.
Authorize only a trusted local administrator. The helper never makes the socket
world-writable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR soju-tui (1),
.BR sojuctl (1),
.BR soju (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The soju-tui contributors.
